# Build context exclusions for agent/ (Week 3 / Task 2.5)
#
# This file now does two jobs, where it used to do one.
#
# 1. Context hygiene, as before: everything not excluded gets tarred up and
#    shipped to the Docker daemon on every build. agent/venv is ~568 MB of dead
#    weight, and agent/.env holds live API keys that have no business crossing
#    into the daemon at all.
#
# 2. Deciding what ships. The Dockerfile used to COPY a hand-written list of
#    filenames, which meant exclusion was encoded in two places; the list was
#    forgotten twice (kb_loader.py, tools.py) while this file was never wrong.
#    The Dockerfile now does `COPY *.py ./`, so THIS is the only place that
#    decides what reaches the image. A new module ships by default — list it
#    below if it should not.

# --- Secrets. Keep this rule first; nothing below should ever override it. ---
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- Virtualenv: ~568 MB, and Linux containers can't use a macOS venv anyway ---
venv/

# --- Python bytecode / packaging litter ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store

# --- Week 2 latency + diagnostic harness --------------------------------------
# Superseded by the telephony server. week2_latency_observer.py is deliberately
# NOT listed: bot.py imports it when NXLYR_LATENCY_CSV is set, so it ships.
test_pipeline.py
test_pipeline_timed.py
test_tone.py
turn_diagnostic.py
analyze_week2.py
backfill_ttfb.py
stt_accuracy_test.py
list_audio_devices.py
check_dotenv.py
entrypoint.sh
wavs/
keycheck/

# --- Dev-only modules that COPY *.py would otherwise pull in ------------------
# Previously kept out of the image by the Dockerfile's explicit COPY list rather
# than by any rule here. Now that the COPY is a wildcard, they need naming.
# prompt_harness.py imports bot and tools and would work in the image, but it is
# a text-mode test driver — there is no reason for it on a production host.
prompt_harness.py
prompt_harness_transcripts/
test_kb_loader.py
mock_exotel_client.py

# --- Shell tooling: host/server inspection, never runs inside the container ---
*.sh

# --- Measurement output and scratch artifacts ---------------------------------
# The .bak / .pre_sanity_check_backup suffixes sit *after* .csv, so a bare
# *.csv rule misses them — hence the explicit trailing-suffix patterns.
*.csv
*.csv.*
*.log
*.bak
snapshot_before.txt
LATENCY_RESULTS.md

# --- Docker's own files: no reason to ship them into their own build ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
